Changes to TKJT (PyOpenJt 21faef4) for the 3D Viewer. Applied by wasm/scripts/build-jt-deps.sh.

- JT 10 (ISO 14306-4) reading, verified on NX-written 10.3 and 10.5 files:
  one-byte element version numbers (JtData_Reader::ReadVersion), removed reserved fields
  (Partition, Base Shape, LOD), Partition version byte, late-loaded property v2 without the
  reserved field, base attribute field-final flags, full RGBA materials, the embedded element
  header before TopoMesh data, single 32-bit "Face Attribute Mask 8" array, BitLengthCodec3T
  (nibbler) bit-length codec, JT 10 probability contexts with escape flags and optional
  out-of-band data, binary (raw IEEE-754) vertex coordinates/normals, Move-to-Front codec.
- JT_PROP_MEASUREMENT_UNITS is recorded (JtData_Model::MeasurementUnits).
- Robustness: corrupt TopoMesh splits throw instead of reading out of bounds (ISO 14306
  Annex E check missing in TKJT); LoadBytes pads buffers since bit readers read whole words.
- zlib: stop at Z_STREAM_END (TechSoft3D JT 8.1 compressed sizes include a trailing byte, which
  made the inflate loop spin forever), and only warn when a compressed stream runs past the
  declared segment end (the same writer declares segments one byte short).

